# HARD RULE — Google Play end goal

FlareCare must be built so it can **pass Google Play review cleanly**.

## Positioning

- **Not** a medical, clinical, diagnostic, or treatment app.
- Do **not** advertise (store listing, screenshots, titles, in-app copy) as giving medical advice or replacing clinicians.
- Personal IBD companion / organiser: track, prepare, navigate everyday life.

## Product

- No invented medical advice or freestyle triage.
- Health/legal claims only from named UK sources (see health/legal hard rule).
- Store listing + Data safety must match what the app actually does.

When copy might sound “medical,” ask Simon before shipping.

## Play Store requirements (tell Simon early)

Full list: **`docs/play-store-requirements.md`**. Also summarized in `apps/mobile/DEV_NOTES.md` → **Play Store requirements**. Biggest current risk: **public Privacy Policy URL** (domain / Vercel) must be live before Console listing — in-app legal alone is not enough.

Also recorded in `apps/mobile/DEV_NOTES.md` (top) and `FEATURES.md`.
